## Lore

Lord Kryygorth was once among the mightiest of the Splugorth and a master of Bio-Wizardry, creator of thousands of organisms. When rivals toppled him he took most of his secrets down with him; only about a dozen of his species survived, among them the Kryygorth Hunters, the Shellbacks, the K-Pegasus and the Lessons.

The Kryygorth Hunter is a vicious, semi-humanoid reptilian predator, once the undisputed ruler of its forest and jungle homeworld until Kryygorth enslaved its kind. Constantly hunched and ready to spring, it fights with razor claws, powerful jaws and a long prehensile tail, leaps 30 feet, and tracks prey by scent and nightvision through the thickest brush or darkest night. Its green and brown hide is natural camouflage. Kryygorth''s Bio-Wizards gave the once purely animal predator heightened intelligence and psionic powers, so it now tells friend from foe, learns a few human-level skills and tactics, tracks creatures of magic and can turn invisible at will.

Slavers buy them for their hunting skill and savagery. They are hard to control but worth the effort, and free Hunters often ally with feral Dog Boys, wild Psi-Stalkers, Simvan and other primitive or aggressive peoples and intelligent predators. Habitat: forests and jungles, but anywhere the Splugorth are.

## Value

A trained Kryygorth Hunter sells for an average 3D6x100,000 credits; one with a history of loyalty, high attributes or M.D.C., or high experience sells for two to three times as much, sometimes more.
